From 47033529c9483433fdddf5917fca9058c93ee975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:32:10 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(ai): honest cost accounting, hard monthly budget
 ceiling, safer streaming

- OpenRouter: request usage accounting and record the real usage.cost + the engine that actually
  answered; failed upstream calls are now logged (status + body snippet, never the key); a
  mid-stream failure/timeout returns the text already shown instead of starting a second answer
- cost: engine-pricing computeRequestCost() prefers provider cost; "free" registry models that run
  on paid OpenRouter engines are priced conservatively instead of $0 (limits never triggered before)
- double-pass: draft cost is no longer counted twice, both passes count toward the token quota,
  the draft call has its own timeout, and it is skipped for code (a "make it concise" rewrite
  breaks code)
- budget: evaluateBudget() stages normal/soft/exhausted/hard_stop; at 100% everything is routed
  to the cheapest engine, at 125% requests are rejected (no more unbounded "unlimited")
- streaming: stream watchdog (first token / idle / total) replaces the single 25 s timer that cut
  every long answer; timed-out partial answers are marked continuable
- circuit breaker is keyed per provider+engine, so one 429 from a free model no longer disables
  every OpenRouter model for 30 s
- Plus "burst" in Auto no longer fails with "requires Pro"

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012JQZ5kjDAEncyyErFsiwm8
