From 7a83a8ed086ecd2110731558dbc2124174706206 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:36:17 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(workspace): code-safe context, query-aware project
 context with plan budgets, safe cache
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- context: cleanText no longer strips indentation / repeated spaces from code (fenced, unclosed
  fence, or pasted indented blocks) — models saw Python/YAML without structure and replace.targetContent
  could never match
- workspace-context: new builder — content budget by plan, model window and input price; files
  picked by relevance to the question (stable core first for provider prefix caching); explicit
  truncation markers; secrets (.env, keys, credentials) never sent; honest instructions instead of
  "FULL ACCESS" and a "do not invent unseen files" rule
- attachments: images and binary documents (PDF/DOCX read as text) no longer injected as garbage;
  the model is told what it cannot see
- gateway: only the last message's project counts (no stale metadata after unlinking); responses
  that depend on a project/attachments are never read from or written to the shared answer cache;
  only finishReason "stop" answers are cached
- payload guard: attachment limit counts only the current request (no cumulative 400 after 10
  files, no double counting); linked project size is capped
- conversation store: file contents are not persisted in message history

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
