From 4dd1cb218a1d88015e9ec71be72997565ebb5450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:48:49 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(workspace): safe file edits, honest attachments,
 continue button

Frontend, project/file work:
- patch-parser: a failed `replace` no longer overwrites the file with the snippet.
  Edits are validated (path traversal, .git, absolute paths, secrets), several
  edits of one file are applied sequentially and merged, rejected edits are shown
  to the user with a reason. Aider path precedence bug fixed; ``` inside file
  contents no longer terminates a file-actions block.
- local/git writers re-apply `replace` edits to the CURRENT file (disk / commit),
  not the in-memory snapshot; commit aborts atomically if a fragment is missing.
- local folder paths are relative to the project root (no more `proj/proj/...`),
  secrets (.env, keys) are never read or sent; stored files are flagged
  `truncated` and never edited by `replace` or shown to the model as whole.
- attachments: DOCX/XLSX/PPTX text is extracted in the browser; PDF and binary
  formats are no longer read as garbage text; composer shows what the model sees.
- GitHub reader: ranked file selection, private repos via token, size limits.
- "Continue" button for replies cut by length/timeout (finishReason/canContinue).
- server: honour `truncated` flag in the project prompt block.

Tests: file-safety, office-text, workspace-paths, extended file-operations.

